    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.listening_items, $seed${"slug":"c2-weigh-an-extreme-case-at-a-panel","title":"Weigh an extreme case at a panel","level":"C2","status":"published","sort_order":200,"metadata":{"format":"dialogue","script_type":"dialogue","speakers":["Moderator","Analyst"]},"summary":"A moderator and analyst distinguish a memorable case from evidence about frequency.","transcript_text":"Moderator: The audience remembers the one cooperative that collapsed after expanding delivery. Doesn't that discredit the recommendation?\nAnalyst: The example matters, but not because a single failure estimates the failure rate. It reveals a mechanism the survey missed. When orders are spread over a wider area, drivers spend longer between stops, and the organisation may lose the social contact that persuaded people to place regular orders.\nModerator: So is the case an exception or a warning?\nAnalyst: It could be both. We should test the mechanism in more cooperatives, including ones that expanded successfully. Otherwise we risk explaining the visible failure after the fact and calling the explanation a policy.\nModerator: Then the recommendation would depend on the conditions we can verify.\nAnalyst: Yes. Where an organisation can preserve route density and contact with members, expansion is a different proposition.","category":"Academic","accent":"general","speed_label":"natural","speed_wpm":150,"duration_seconds":56,"audio_url":null,"focus_skill":"inference","tags":["academic","dialogue"],"questions":[{"id":"q1","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the most important contribution of the failed case?","options":["It settles how often all cooperatives fail","It demonstrates that no successful expansions exist","It exposes a possible mechanism to investigate","It proves the recommendation must be abandoned"],"answer_index":2,"explanation":"The analyst values the case for surfacing a plausible link between wider routes, contact and repeat orders."},{"id":"q2","type":"mcq","prompt":"Why include successful expansions in the next study?","options":["To check when the proposed mechanism does and does not apply","To replace the case with a more optimistic story","To prove that failures cannot produce useful evidence","To avoid collecting information about routes"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"Successes are needed to test whether preserving contact and route density changes the outcome."},{"id":"q3","type":"mcq","prompt":"What is the analyst's final position?","options":["Expansion should proceed whenever one cooperative succeeds","The recommendation should depend on verifiable operating conditions","All explanations after a failure are equally strong","Policy should answer the latest audience question first"],"answer_index":1,"explanation":"The conclusion makes the advice conditional on demonstrated route density and contact."}]}$seed$::jsonb) r
