    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b1-embedded-questions-at-the-help-desk","title":"Embedded questions at the maker space help desk","level":"B1","status":"published","sort_order":320,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"embedded-questions","explanation_text":"At the maker space help desk, you can ask a direct question such as “Where are the clamps?” You can also put the question inside a longer one: “Could you tell me where the clamps are?” Keep the question word, then use statement order in the part that comes after it: subject before verb. If the direct question uses do, does, or did to form the question, drop that helping verb and put the main verb in the right form.\n\nFor a yes-or-no question, start the embedded part with if or whether and use statement order: “Do you know if the workshop is open?” When the question word is itself the subject, keep it before the verb: “Who checks the bookings?” becomes “Do you know who checks the bookings?”\n\nLook at the whole sentence to choose the end punctuation. “Could you tell me where the clamps are?” is a question. “I’d like to know where the clamps are.” is a statement.","contrast_text":"Compare the direct question “When does the tool room close?” with “Do you know when the tool room closes?” In the embedded part, the tool room comes before closes, and the main verb takes the -s.","common_error_pattern":"A common error is keeping direct-question order or keeping do, does, or did as a question helper inside the embedded part. In “Could you tell me where is the glue?”, change “where is the glue” to “where the glue is”.","examples_json":[{"bad":"Could you tell me where are the spare batteries?","good":"Could you tell me where the spare batteries are?"},{"bad":"Do you know does the tool room have a first aid kit?","good":"Do you know whether the tool room has a first aid kit?"},{"bad":"Can you tell me how often does the attendant check the safety forms?","good":"Can you tell me how often the attendant checks the safety forms?"},{"bad":"I would like to know when will the next tour start.","good":"I would like to know when the next tour will start."}],"tags":["b1-embedded-questions-at-the-help-desk","embedded questions","indirect questions","statement word order","if and whether","subject questions","question punctuation"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
