    from jsonb_populate_record(null::public.grammar_units, $seed${"slug":"b1-so-and-such-in-event-reviews","title":"So and such in event reviews","level":"B1","status":"published","sort_order":320,"metadata":{},"focus_area":"so-and-such","explanation_text":"Use so before an adjective or adverb to make it stronger. If the hall was so cold, you are describing the hall. If the actors spoke so clearly, you are describing how they spoke.\n\nUse such before a noun phrase. With a singular countable noun, put a or an after such, as in such a lively market or such an unusual display. Choose a or an according to the sound of the next word. With plural nouns and uncountable nouns, leave out a and an, as in such bright lanterns and such loud music. To stress quantity, use so many with plural countable nouns and so much with uncountable nouns.\n\nIn a review, add a clause beginning with that to show what happened as a result. For example, the guide spoke so quietly that people at the back moved closer. The first part tells readers how quietly the guide spoke, and the that clause shows the result.","contrast_text":"Compare The square was so crowded that we left with It was such a crowded square that we left. In the first sentence, crowded stands on its own. In the second, crowded describes the noun square. Compare such bright lights, which describes the lights, with so many lights, which stresses their number.","common_error_pattern":"Use such to emphasize a description within a noun phrase, as in such fresh bread. Use so much or so many for quantity. Use so before an adjective on its own, as in so warm. With a singular countable noun, put a or an after such.","examples_json":[{"bad":"The rehearsal room was such warm that we opened a window.","good":"The rehearsal room was so warm that we opened a window."},{"bad":"It was such unusual lantern display that we stayed until closing time.","good":"It was such an unusual lantern display that we stayed until closing time."},{"bad":"The market sold so fresh bread that we bought another loaf to take home.","good":"The market sold such fresh bread that we bought another loaf to take home."},{"bad":"There were so much people on the guided walk that the guide split us into two groups.","good":"There were so many people on the guided walk that the guide split us into two groups."}],"tags":["B1","b1-so-and-such-in-event-reviews","degree","articles","quantity","result clauses","event reviews"]}$seed$::jsonb) r
