 we recovered’ or ‘the material that we recovered’. Use which to ask for the identity of a member of a set, stated explicitly or understood from context. For example, “determine which of the two exemptions the board granted”.","examples":[{"bad":"The editors published the material what the fact-checkers had verified.","good":"The editors published what the fact-checkers had verified."},{"bad":"Whomever chairs the panel will sign the recommendation.","good":"Whoever chairs the panel will sign the recommendation."},{"bad":"The conservator may use whichever of the two mounts she considers it safer.","good":"The conservator may use whichever of the two mounts she considers safer."},{"bad":"The registrar needs to determine which of the two exemptions did the board grant.","good":"The registrar needs to determine which of the two exemptions the board granted."}]}}$seed$::jsonb) r
